    "verdict": "PASSES S1 and S2: SP-R1a-GP-k11-S2 beats the best per-fold baseline by +77.9% on the mean and +70.1% in its worst fold at n = 80",
    "survival": {
      "S1_mean_margin_at_80_ge_20pct": true,
      "S2_worst_fold_at_80_ge_20pct": true,
      "S3_downstream": "not evaluated here; the per-fold measure and arrays are recorded so the downstream comparison can be made without re-running",
      "headline_arm_by_preregistered_rule": "SP-R1a-GP-k11-S2",
      "headline_arm_frozen_in_plan": "SP-R1a-GP-k11",
      "rule_note": "the pre-registered ranking rule selected SP-R1a-GP-k11-S2 over the plan's frozen SP-R1a-GP-k11; both are reported, and the frozen cell is the one named in the pre-registration so no criterion is moved after the fact",
      "coverage_arbiter": {
        "arm": "SP-R1a-GP-k11-S2",
        "mean_coverage68": 0.008363395863395863,
        "mean_coverage95": 0.01626142376142376,
        "nominal68": 0.68,
        "nominal95": 0.95,
        "arm_judged": "SP-R1a-GP-k11-S2",
        "note": "",
        "calibrated_at_68": false,
        "calibrated_at_95": false,
        "verdict": "the predictive density is UNUSABLE: empirical coverage is 0.8% at the nominal 68% level and 1.6% at 95%, i.e. the intervals are overconfident by orders of magnitude",
        "cause": "the tuning protocol drives the noise variance to the grid floor (n2 = 1e-8) because the output is a deterministic AC solve: the marginal likelihood and held-out error both reward interpolating every training point, which leaves no residual variance for the test rows. The POINT prediction is unaffected, but no downstream use may treat the GP variance as a confidence statement.",
        "nlpd_note": "NLPD is reported but is not read as evidence in either direction: it becomes hugely negative when the density sharpens around a small-but-nonzero error, which is exactly the failure this run already caught once."
      },
      "S4_density_calibrated": false,
